SUMMARY:Dino Dig Live
DESCRIPTION:Every summer the NCMNS paleontology crew goes into the field to search for new fossil specimens and continue digging up previous discoveries. \nJoin us in the SECU Daily Planet Theater in person\, or online\, for a live video call from a dinosaur quarry! Paleontologists from NCMNS will be live from their fossil quarries across the American West searching for clues to ancient life from millions of years ago from Nebraska to Utah. \nJoin us in-person in the SECU Daily Planet Theater or watch the livestream on YouTube Live. \nOur live calls (every week this summer!) will give you the chance to join the expedition. You can ask questions and interact with paleontologists in the field. Watch online at the links below. \n\nNew Mexico on Friday\, May 15\, at 12:00 PM\nNew Mexico on Saturday\, May 23\, at 2:00 PM\nUtah on Friday\, June 5 at 12:00 PM\nUtah on Thursday\, June 18 at 12:00 PM\nUtah on Saturday\, July 11 at 2:00 PM\nUtah on Friday\, July 17\, at 12:00 PM\nNebraska August 5th at 12:00 PM\nMontana on Friday\, August 7 at 12:00 PM
URL:https://www.naturalsciences.org/calendar/event/dino-dig-live-2/2026-07-11/
LOCATION:Nature Research Center\, 121 West Jones Street\, Raleigh\, NC\, 27601\, United States
CATEGORIES:All Ages,General Events,Meet the Scientist,Paleontology,SECU Daily Planet Theater,Virtual,Walk-up Programs
ORGANIZER;CN="Chris%20Smith":MAILTO:christopher.smith@naturalsciences.org
GEO:35.7822405;-78.6409677
