SUMMARY:Nature Stories at NCMA
DESCRIPTION:*This program takes place at the North Carolina Museum of Art. Please meet us near the Welcome Center.* \nOpen your eyes to the wonderful world of nature through a family-friendly\, nature-filled story time. We’ll begin by sharing a story and will then explore natural themes through hands-on\, interactive activities. We may head to other areas of the Art Museum’s campus. \nThis is a free program. Come dressed for the weather and prepared to take a walk. Most walks will be stroller-friendly. Designed for ages 7 & younger – everyone welcome!
URL:https://www.naturalsciences.org/calendar/event/nature-stories-at-ncma/
LOCATION:North Carolina Museum of Art\, 2110 Blue Ridge Rd\, Raleigh\, 27607
CATEGORIES:Children,Nature Stories,Outdoor Experiences,Walk-up Programs
ORGANIZER;CN="Kiersten%20Bowser":MAILTO:kiersten.bowser@naturalsciences.org
END:VEVENT
